      "side": 1,
      "message": "Flag `wait_for_response` indicates that one of extensions is expecting accept/reject message. Usually the flag is set by call to `tcpci_partner_start_sender_response_timer`. When an extension is waiting for accept/reject, common code shouldn\u0027t handle this message and should call extensions handlers instead (because of that `NOT_HANDLED` is returned). When `wait_for_response` is false, common handler is executed i.e. soft reset is send, because message is not expected.\n\nThere is one special case when `wait_for_response` and `in_soft_reset` are true. Then common code is waiting for accept/reject in response to soft reset. In that case common code is handling this message (hard reset in case of reject and stopping sender response timer in case of accept).",
